# GHG Tracker - Feature Expansion Walkthrough

All 4 requested features have been successfully implemented and integrated.

## 1. Scope 2 (Electricity) Calculator
A dedicated calculator for indirect emissions from purchased electricity is now live.
- **Location**: Access via "Emission Calculations" -> "Scope 2" card.
- **Features**: Supports grid-specific emission factors (US regional, UK, EU, Global).
- **Storage**: Automatically saves to the same centralized database as Scope 1.

## 2. Custom Emission Factors
Users can now define their own specific factors for unique equipment.
- **Location**: "Settings" page (top navigation).
- **Features**: Add/Delete factors for CO2, CH4, and N2O.
- **Usage**: Once saved, custom factors appear in the main calculator's "Source/Fuel" dropdown with a ⭐ icon.

## 3. PDF Reports
Professional PDF reports can now be generated directly from the database.
- **Location**: "Emissions Reports" page.
- **Features**: A new "PDF Report" button generates a landscape PDF with company branding, summary totals, and a detailed data table.

## 4. Reduction Targets (Goals)
The Dashboard now includes progress tracking against annual targets.
- **Location**: Dashboard (bottom row).
- **Features**: Set an annual tCO2e target. The system calculates real-time progress against your current year's emissions and displays a color-coded status bar.

## Verification Steps
- [x] **Scope 2**: Verified that MWh inputs are correctly converted to kg CO2e.
- [x] **Custom Factors**: Verified that adding a factor in Settings makes it available in the calculator immediately.
- [x] **PDF**: Verified that the generated report includes correct totals and formatting.
- [x] **Goals**: Verified that updating the goal refreshes the progress bar correctly.

> [!NOTE]
> All data is secured per-user in the backend SQLite databases, matching the existing security model.
